infographic compare-binary-horizontal-underline-text-vs
data
  title Two inner rings, two kinds of rule
  desc Entities hold enterprise-wide invariants; use cases hold this app's process — which is why the billing-hold check belongs in Use Cases, not Entities
  compares
    - label Entities ring (enterprise-wide rules)
      children
        - label True in any app on this business
          desc A mobile app and an ops console reuse the same entities
        - label Order needs at least one line item
          desc An invariant the entity enforces on itself
        - label Invoice total equals sum of line items
          desc Pure in-memory rule, no I/O or services
        - label The most stable inner core
          desc Changes only when the business itself changes
    - label Use Cases ring (application-specific rules)
      children
        - label Specific to this app's process
          desc Different apps on the same domain differ here
        - label Confirm order, then check billing hold
          desc The ordered steps to generate an invoice
        - label Orchestrates entities and services
          desc Consults IBillingHoldChecker, repositories
        - label Shared app logic lives here
          desc CheckBillingHoldService sits in this ring
theme
  palette #6366f1 #14b8a6
